<item>
  <title>A reproducible analysis template I actually use</title>
  <dc:creator>Tareq Al-Ahdal</dc:creator>
  <link>https://alahdalta1.github.io/posts/welcome/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<p>Most analysis projects rot because nobody can re-run them six months later. Here’s the skeleton I start every project with so that <code>make all</code> reproduces everything from raw data to the figures in the paper.</p>
<section id="the-layout" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-layout">The layout</h2>
<pre><code>project/
├── data/
│   ├── raw/          # never edited by hand
│   └── derived/      # everything here is regenerated
├── R/                # functions, sourced not run top-to-bottom
├── analysis/         # numbered scripts: 01_clean.R, 02_model.R ...
├── figures/
├── renv.lock         # pinned R dependencies
├── Makefile
└── README.md</code></pre>
</section>
<section id="the-rule-that-makes-it-work" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-rule-that-makes-it-work">The rule that makes it work</h2>
<p>Raw data is read-only. Everything in <code>data/derived/</code> is produced by a script and can be deleted and rebuilt at any time. If you can’t delete it and get it back, it doesn’t belong there.</p>
</section>
<section id="a-tiny-makefile" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="a-tiny-makefile">A tiny Makefile</h2>
<p>```makefileall: figures/fig1.png</p>
<p>data/derived/clean.rds: analysis/01_clean.R data/raw/source.csv Rscript $&lt;</p>
<p>figures/fig1.png: analysis/02_model.R data/derived/clean.rds Rscript $&lt; ```</p>
<p>Make only re-runs what changed. Touch the cleaning script and just the downstream steps rebuild.</p>
<p><em>Example post — swap for your own content.</em></p>


</section>

